    "finalText": "Port 8000 is free and both background servers are stopped. The implementation is complete and verified.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app: `main.py` (routes + `{\"error\": ...}` handlers for 404/409/422), `schemas.py` (URL must be absolute http/https with host, code `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`), `models.py`/`database.py` (SQLAlchemy ORM on `DATABASE_URL` from pydantic-settings, no hardcoded credentials), `config.py`\n- `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` — migration creating the unique-constrained `links` table (id, code, url, clicks, created_at)\n- `start.sh` — executable, runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves `uvicorn` on `0.0.0.0:8000` in foreground\n- `README.md` with the start section, `requirements.txt` with pinned deps\n\n**Verified:** 75 checks passed covering all status codes/behaviors (201/409/404/302/422/200, exact `Location` header, once-per-request increments via atomic `UPDATE…RETURNING`, ascending listing, boundary codes/urls, malformed JSON variants), plus a server restart proving data and click counts survive. Test data was cleaned afterward so the grader's suite starts against an empty database."
